{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966789,"nonce":"xBgrqPICpM7JfZc0pxk8jG/95Z0=","title":"effects on methods landed upstream, but the fix was to call the FSM's emitted reader fn,","message":"RESOLVED. Upstream 186f836 gave impl items annotations and made the\nimpl lowering derive effects from them, so `@effect(E)` on a method\nworks. Annotating the view still did not make the op resolve, and the\nanswer was simpler: the FSM pass already emits\n`\u003cFsm\u003e$readid_\u003cfield\u003e`, a free function declaring the effect whose body\nperforms the op. A read calls THAT. An ordinary call, resolved against\nwhichever handler is installed where it runs.\n\nThe original constraint, kept because it explains the shape:\n\nAn effect operation resolves only inside a function that DECLARES the\neffect. `TypedFunction` has `effects: Vec\u003cInternedString\u003e`;\n`TypedMethod` does not. A Blinc `component X { view { … } }` lowers to\nan inherent impl (the grammar picked that shape because inherent\nlowering mangles methods as `Type$method`, which is the `X$view` symbol\nthe host calls). So a view cannot say it performs its FSM's effect, and\n`Dial$id_level()` fails to lower with \"Call to undefined function\".\n\n**Why it matters:** that op call is the in-language way to resolve a\ncontext field's signal for the mount whose handler is installed. Without\nit the host does the lookup, keyed by FSM name off the install stack.\nWorks, but it is the last name-keyed step in the read path.\n\n**Upstream patch:** add `effects` to `TypedMethod` and thread it through\nthe inherent-impl lowering that already mangles a method into a\nfunction. A method is a function by HIR, so the plumbing point exists.\n\n**Local alternative:** emit a component's view as a top-level\n`fn \u003cComp\u003e$view` rather than an inherent impl. Wider than it sounds:\n`bind_component_props`, the `__component_props__` marker and stateful\ndetection all key on the impl shape.\n\nRelated: [[feedback-no-hashmap-between-runtimes]].","files":null}]}